# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Large, regenerable model artifacts (72M) -- reconstructed by
# `make reproduce-full` (scripts/42, 58, 78, etc.); not needed for
# `make audit`/`make test`/`make reproduce` (the fast path), which is why
# scripts/audit_provenance.py explicitly excludes out/models/*.pt already.
out/models/*.pt

# Large frozen-embedding caches (146M in data/, ~145M duplicated into
# package/data/licensed/ for the licensing quarantine) -- regenerable via
# scripts/61_fm_embeddings.py. Excluded from git for repo-size hygiene, not
# for licensing reasons (DNABERT-2 is Apache-2.0, PromoGen2 is CC-BY-NC-4.0,
# both permit redistribution -- the quarantine directory structure and
# LICENSE files documenting this are still tracked, only the .npz payloads
# are excluded).
data/fm_embeddings/*.npz
package/data/licensed/*/*.npz

# Johns et al. 2018 article and supplementary materials -- Springer Nature /
# Nature Methods copyright (see crosshost-PROJECT-CHARTER.md Part V, "do not
# re-host raw tables without checking"). This project does not hold
# redistribution rights, and availability on PMC under the NIH Public Access
# Policy is not a redistribution licence.
#
# KEPT, for provenance-audit purposes only: nihms945382_bodytext.txt (47 KB,
# the extracted body text used as a unit-test fixture by scripts/03 and
# scripts/15), the five main-text figure thumbnails, and the two smallest xlsx
# supplements (-6, 46 KB and -7, 14 KB).
#
# EXCLUDED, as the bulkier and more directly re-hostable items: the full author
# manuscript (nihms945382.pdf, 1.2 MB) and its full text in XML
# (nihms945382.nxml), the three large xlsx supplements (-3, -4, -5; 21.4 MB
# combined), the supplementary-text docx, and the bundled PMC tarball.
#
# Supplements 3-5 were tracked until Gate 34 and the pdf/nxml until Gate 35,
# contrary to the policy above. They remain in earlier commits and in the v1.0.0
# Zenodo archive; history was deliberately not rewritten, because that would
# break the correspondence between this repository and the DOI cited in the
# manuscript. A v1.0.1 release drops them going forward.
#
# Obtain independently from PMC (PMC6065261) or Nature Methods
# (doi:10.1038/nmeth.4633) before running `make reproduce-full`'s Gate-1/2
# stage. `make reproduce` (the fast path) reads none of them.
raw/NIHMS945382-supplement-2.docx
raw/NIHMS945382-supplement-3.xlsx
raw/NIHMS945382-supplement-4.xlsx
raw/NIHMS945382-supplement-5.xlsx
raw/nihms945382.pdf
raw/nihms945382.nxml
raw/PMC6065261.tar.gz

# mmseqs2 clustering intermediates (85M) -- regenerated by
# scripts/19_mmseqs_clustering.py, not read by any fast-path script.
raw/mmseqs/

# DRAFTS (Gate 10) source-data bundles -- fully redundant with the
# individually-extracted files kept alongside them (same pattern as the
# Johns et al. PMC tarball exclusion above). PMC6692573.tar.gz (48M) bundles
# every other raw/drafts/ file; msb198875_SourceData_Appendix.zip (20M)
# bundles per-appendix-figure source data that duplicates the per-figure
# xlsx files scripts/88-92 actually read. Neither is read by any committed
# script. Both hashes remain in data/MANIFEST.json for provenance even
# though the bytes aren't tracked -- obtain via the URL recorded there.
raw/drafts/PMC6692573.tar.gz
raw/drafts/msb198875_SourceData_Appendix.zip

# Ad-hoc background-job stdout logs, not committed artifacts
out/gate8_5_*.log
out/gate8_6_*.log

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local Claude Code session state, not project content
.claude/
out.zip
